{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0b823cb54ca3e16b3bc83d065b8a0b69569b469f57e00bb763aa81520ba0c97d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"yc-software/qm@361a6c0095dc snapshot da4f0a633de29ba8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_16b3d9034201340ff23a6dacc60754695fc4ae899e31b79c6e1abc70fd5ac0e3"],"source_ids":["src_352b0e355cbd54268718831d36e39e0e"],"text":"The deployment config root requires contract: 1, orgId, publicUrl, target, and a services list including core; target is docker, fly, or aws, and unknown contract majors fail closed.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0d76cf275a7ab00269188349f6ed6b173d09fa3946a2a3c36026c0c450792ba6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"yc-software/qm@361a6c0095dc snapshot da4f0a633de29ba8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_be5b29eb066d0ddfec8394919f4a83dbfcc764d76ec65f08d0e6075c8f6ffe5f","slc_f36d83ebe6898648de4944fcaac023d0367ecd575d2d308551096dd2779213b5"],"source_ids":["src_aa7699a5d8a05d50b92ea81e54e642c3"],"text":"Without DATABASE_URL and SESSION_STORE=postgres, sessions live in process memory and vanish on restart; Postgres otherwise holds user data, session history, and durable state.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1d5847e861a37f4714dd5d00d846e7b7da4cd4e41e6f7fa42521b4556afb6dac","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"yc-software/qm@361a6c0095dc snapshot da4f0a633de29ba8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1fe59d64902e00954e73378234d1630d8187ea03c215ee6f5f35354306126547"],"source_ids":["src_aa7699a5d8a05d50b92ea81e54e642c3"],"text":"The core runs TypeScript directly on Node with Fastify for HTTP; the Slack plugin uses Bolt, and the web UI builds with Vite and renders with Lit.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_29aa8bc90c4bf89f650bd770b65d2349abdf5faa8c416e6bf36e6e42e4c38eac","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"yc-software/qm@361a6c0095dc snapshot da4f0a633de29ba8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3a49cbf23ef448b1c925c6690a39b156b62ad082ad98b566d5eccd6e340152e1"],"source_ids":["src_aa7699a5d8a05d50b92ea81e54e642c3"],"text":"Repository development practice: contributions are accepted as human-written text, not code — contributors describe changes informally in a .txt or .md file under adrs/, and maintainers handle implementation; vulnerabilities are reported privately.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2d3163258b3cb69d281475a7278c4258dc53f6d95f2bd230ba8cca327ec5cafe","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"yc-software/qm@361a6c0095dc snapshot da4f0a633de29ba8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_bc9cfc99907859865f2ae0f155d8e48169e4cde114fa03d7d7406a6ddc0bfec8","slc_fc0e1f6267960653cc5dfec07d9df75b8797225d5419297bc9695e686a521a53"],"source_ids":["src_aa7699a5d8a05d50b92ea81e54e642c3"],"text":"Each person and each room gets its own scoped memory, files, keychain view, permissions, crons, web apps, and durable sandbox, so employees work independently while collaborating in channels and projects.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_43e6a44524b7999ec69c6d1db772b7d4218d73c0c963af9c71d73aab299ba7b2","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"yc-software/qm@361a6c0095dc snapshot da4f0a633de29ba8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6a079f9c502679ecb29637401128d9ea44ced1c4a7349d55e9bf477767d1aa90","slc_df66acb1a36b7c13b20a473be59aa6497dcfcabcb0a540a9adf9c7e3d91a4e8a"],"source_ids":["src_352b0e355cbd54268718831d36e39e0e","src_aa7699a5d8a05d50b92ea81e54e642c3"],"text":"Deployments depend on the @yc-software/qm package; the deployment directory's package.json pins the engine at the exact scaffolding version so the directory records which CLI interprets it.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5c836b847b7e0f4edbd516f67e78bbcaa02aea4a7251d2238130b83df29470eb","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"yc-software/qm@361a6c0095dc snapshot da4f0a633de29ba8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_f36d83ebe6898648de4944fcaac023d0367ecd575d2d308551096dd2779213b5"],"source_ids":["src_aa7699a5d8a05d50b92ea81e54e642c3"],"text":"Every turn runs through a central core that can use various models and harnesses; the agent has a small fixed tool surface, including execute, which runs commands in the scope's own durable isolated sandbox.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5e0d041a5aa6b71618416834fe147649eb2775be6a8cabd03377f5bc14518709","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=relevance","setting":"yc-software/qm@361a6c0095dc snapshot da4f0a633de29ba8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_cf047d57b8e9665115eda2341021be73b7c689873192883c12eecb3f4748a198","slc_fc0e1f6267960653cc5dfec07d9df75b8797225d5419297bc9695e686a521a53"],"source_ids":["src_aa7699a5d8a05d50b92ea81e54e642c3"],"text":"QM targets startups wanting a company-wide agent: employees get isolated workspaces, collaborate in Slack channels and projects, and the same identity and configuration carries between Slack and the web app.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6284ad912d5f8d58ab3fc76e9db43e1121b25f194b38616f8471c51827bb3907","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"yc-software/qm@361a6c0095dc snapshot da4f0a633de29ba8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_ed0beb8a8db27b673f3be26e78556a861f8d45c3b7a889122b04a98e4b5cc4ee"],"source_ids":["src_14ea236fd30f549f8f8853f8a22682b9"],"text":"Admin model verification's small probe does not certify prices, maximum advertised context/output limits, image support, every reasoning level, or correct tool execution; admin-managed API models remain Pi-only in normal use.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7d53517883f87e7e9e6ee152531f4f1d1daabcdc0b641fc3592e3057630dafb3","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"yc-software/qm@361a6c0095dc snapshot da4f0a633de29ba8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_a98ee97779e603d260ff608b7b608510f755c4af7e8f62dab89a36f219b4327b"],"source_ids":["src_352b0e355cbd54268718831d36e39e0e"],"text":"Repository development practice: the normal deployment gate order is check, doctor, plan, up --yes, then check --live, with infra build-image preceding plan on AWS MicroVM sandboxes.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8408746c8d3f5d30f6274d9328670bc6678f2b5d2655b0a91a5389df213a2c69","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"yc-software/qm@361a6c0095dc snapshot da4f0a633de29ba8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_933eadb58aba7a9d4fbdec37df466d10265a4ea9b7e43c9c4d4297f7b3dbbea9"],"source_ids":["src_aa7699a5d8a05d50b92ea81e54e642c3"],"text":"In Open sharing posture, included memories are loaded into the prompt in full with source-scope labels and are searchable, with no relevance ranking applied; the candidate window is 100 recent sessions and 200 files.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8681a067b467fd47e2bde2d6a36c3bb3bd0cb42ea0d43cb35de964aaecb31ff5","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"yc-software/qm@361a6c0095dc snapshot da4f0a633de29ba8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_696954c49ec94ab45a5c0391922960aa37cc9fa0f3a66a9f24831fc8a58fb4f4"],"source_ids":["src_55ee532709e2527a9097030284bfac39"],"text":"A deployment runs three application workloads: core, web-ui (chat plus admin under /admin), and portal, which is the public entry point and hosts the optional built-in auth broker; Slack stays in core.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8947e8289a18c308863022fa4ba22b2954b24763433d2e5e7c71e68cb1e387de","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"yc-software/qm@361a6c0095dc snapshot da4f0a633de29ba8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2e77f95769e995b70c7d9ffa5584a2e67cbf8cc97afb6be7675882038fc4863c"],"source_ids":["src_aa7699a5d8a05d50b92ea81e54e642c3"],"text":"A predeclared command policy with approval rules and hard denials for destructive operations like recursive deletes applies in every posture, including Dangerous.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8e36d303fb7c3b7f02885e59915a461e7de307cfd6239f856b89aa63e80b906a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"yc-software/qm@361a6c0095dc snapshot da4f0a633de29ba8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_748869fdb4e799b56b6889211ab40c5a4e5d2e6b6319505c3d93aff254d3d945"],"source_ids":["src_352b0e355cbd54268718831d36e39e0e"],"text":"Published apps receive AGENT_API_URL and AGENT_CREDENTIAL_TOKEN and call $AGENT_API_URL/v1/credentials/broker with the token in x-agent-capability, authorizing as the immutable publisher rather than the viewing person.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_bc394e17d63d26b10dcec08cac4001456b5f19e3fcb1c1561f02e943025dd2fe","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"yc-software/qm@361a6c0095dc snapshot da4f0a633de29ba8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1461335969dcd4c0c23c3214cc7c05fa8c8a6e847cc5dfe029bdfa0a37a505c9","slc_4d56aa2cf662347311454134613bb3cf59080670165d3598c10480885957d421","slc_6bfae010cfba221fd5dff96c5f186bc3306be5f3d934616c76e347dc0dea7347","slc_aea2b5ea6d9a52e1523da6efa21819eb1de49a545d80d0928385c2b5bb43df63"],"source_ids":["src_352b0e355cbd54268718831d36e39e0e"],"text":"The security screen proxy contract specifies HTTPS POSTs with a JSON body carrying text, hook (user_input or tool_response), and chunk metadata; providers return score and threshold in 0..1 plus an optional primary_outcome label.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c341709600308201865df64c31a5134c6de266aded16baee1cdd5b230a20ab34","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"yc-software/qm@361a6c0095dc snapshot da4f0a633de29ba8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_fbce4da5329621557e377342f6aff33196bff581304ead4e5fd4ee0d2d5c64a0"],"source_ids":["src_352b0e355cbd54268718831d36e39e0e"],"text":"Contract v1 defines a committed, portable deployment directory whose sole interpreter is the qm CLI, which validates the same inputs it uses to render containers, task definitions, secret routing, and the agent-computer layer.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c773afaf2ffa741e5aa121747236680e3d16a014ecd9c10f95180112a860bc8c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"yc-software/qm@361a6c0095dc snapshot da4f0a633de29ba8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1893eb30e43bcf9c1ac4157263c796a56164e215ccfa3c3b057a13b3a04a5785","slc_a4bba3a5ab84a558316a930b9fe31838c4dca29f44ec534b722bfe345f72fb1f"],"source_ids":["src_aa7699a5d8a05d50b92ea81e54e642c3"],"text":"Orgs pick one security posture — Strict (human approval per tool call), Auto (default; classifier screens provenance-labelled external data), or Dangerous (no screening or pauses) — and narrower scopes can only tighten it.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_eb912c2843273e979dd2af371249a486799ed49a714c7ecdb915181ae3d13305","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"yc-software/qm@361a6c0095dc snapshot da4f0a633de29ba8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2d30c2556ce979f54394065076e968230d5a04d8a791243c43d034fce7b2b609"],"source_ids":["src_aa7699a5d8a05d50b92ea81e54e642c3"],"text":"The core is generic: org-specific config, tools, skills, sandbox image, and infrastructure live in a deployment directory, and every substrate (harness, session store, sandbox, memory) sits behind an interface.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:24:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6298d4fca4ce4ad08b9ec1c6739f6e55"}
